#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# parametric_region

#% text
# `parametric_region([f1, f2, ...], [[u, a, b], ...])` is the set of points `(f1, f2, ...)` as the parameters run over their ranges.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The measure is the integral of the length, area or volume element over the parameters.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Half of the unit circle:

#% cell
c = parametric_region([cos(t), sin(t)], [[t, 0, pi]])

#% text
# Its length:

#% cell
region_measure(c)
#% output
#= pi

#% text
# Its bounds:

#% cell
region_bounds(c)
#% output
#= [[-1.0, 1.0], [0.0, 1.0]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `implicit_region`, `region_integrate`
